# 12. SYNCHRONIZATION LAB — PRODUCER CONSUMER

Create a visual Producer–Consumer simulation using a bounded buffer.

This must be one of the most impressive interactive pages.

### Simulation components

- Producer threads.
- Consumer threads.
- Fixed-size buffer.
- Mutex lock.
- Empty semaphore.
- Full semaphore.

### Functionality

Allow the user to:
- Start producers.
- Start consumers.
- Pause execution.
- Resume execution.
- Reset the simulation.
- Adjust buffer capacity.
- Adjust producer speed.
- Adjust consumer speed.

Visualize items entering and leaving the buffer.

Show:
- Current buffer occupancy.
- Empty slots.
- Full slots.
- Mutex status.
- Semaphore counts.
- Producer state.
- Consumer state.

### Synchronization rules

- A producer must wait when the buffer is full.
- A consumer must wait when the buffer is empty.
- Only one thread can enter the critical section at a time.
- Buffer operations must be protected by synchronization logic.

Display an event log such as:

"Producer P1 waiting for an empty slot."

"Producer P1 acquired mutex."

"Item inserted into buffer."

"Consumer C1 acquired mutex."

"Item consumed successfully."

"Mutex released."

Use a proper simulation state machine. Do not merely animate random items.

The user must be able to understand why synchronization is necessary.

